  "body": "From the review of PR #141 (#107), unverified (no Mac on hand). winit's default macOS app menu has a Quit item that probably ends the process without going through the guarded Quit command or the close path, so the Save / Don't Save / Cancel prompt would be skipped. OS logoff/shutdown also kills the app with no prompt (winit doesn't report it) - same family.\n\nDone means: on macOS, Cmd+Q and the app-menu Quit route through the guarded Quit command (replace or hook the default menu item), checked on a Mac by a contributor.",
